// COREL meaning-postulate grammar (subset), after Arcas Túnez (2008), section 3.1.7.2.
//
//   +(e1: +BE_00 (x1: +BIRD_00)Theme (x2: +VERTEBRATE_00)Referent)
//   *(e2: +COMPRISE_00 (x1)Theme (x3: m +FEATHER_00 & 2 +LEG_00 & 2 +WING_00)Referent)
//   *((e3: +COMPRISE_00 (x1)Theme (x4: 2 +LEG_00)Referent) (e4: +BE_01 (x4)Theme (x5: +LONG_00)Attribute))
//   +(e9: n +FLY_00 (x1)Agent (x1)Theme (x10)Origin (x11)Goal)
//
// Covered: reasoning operators (+ strict, * defeasible), linked predications,
// predication operators (aspect, tense, modality, polarity), arguments (x) and
// satellites (f), selection preferences with quantifiers and the connectors & | ^,
// predications as fillers of satellites/arguments, connectors between participants.
// Also covered after the real export (P03): coreferent variables as fillers ((f3: x1)Scene),
// negated selection preferences ((f1: n +PERMISSION_00)Manner) and parenthesised groups of
// linked predications as satellite fillers. Not covered: the lambda connector.

?start: postulate

postulate: item+

item: REASON_OP predication                -> free_item
    | REASON_OP "(" predication+ ")"        -> linked_item

predication: "(" EVAR ":" pred_op* concept participants? ")"

pred_op: ASPECT | TENSE | MODALITY | POLARITY

participants: participant (CONNECTOR? participant)*

participant: "(" PVAR (":" filler)? ")" ROLE

?filler: sel_expr
       | predication (CONNECTOR? predication)*  -> pred_filler
       | "(" predication+ ")"                   -> pred_filler

?sel_expr: sel_term (CONNECTOR sel_term)*  -> sel_group

?sel_term: POLARITY? QUANT? concept         -> sel_concept
         | PVAR                                -> sel_var
         | "(" sel_expr ")"

concept: CONCEPT

REASON_OP: "+" | "*"
EVAR: /e\d+/
PVAR: /[xf]\d+/
ASPECT.2: "ing" | "pro" | "egr"
TENSE.2: "rpast" | "past" | "npast" | "pres" | "nfut" | "fut" | "rfut"
MODALITY.2: "cert" | "prob" | "pos" | "obl" | "adv" | "perm"
POLARITY.2: "n"
QUANT.2: /\d+/ | "m" | "s" | "p" | "i"
CONNECTOR: "&" | "|" | "^"
CONCEPT.3: /[#+$][A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*/ | /[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*(?![a-z])/
ROLE: /[A-Z][a-z]+/

%import common.WS
%ignore WS
